    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d699">

                <pb facs="0665" n="653" xml:id="pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115 European War 1939/164: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-01T18:00:00+00:00">December 1, 1939—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 1—2:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following from Berlin via Brussels, 250, December 1, 11 a.m.</p>
                <p>From Berlin.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>236, November 30, 6 p.m. Notify Foreign Office and repeat to Department. In
                        memorandum dated November 28 German Foreign Office has informed Embassy that
                        French and British nationals in territory occupied by Germany will receive
                        substantially the same treatment as enemy aliens in Germany itself.
                        Permission to depart from Germany will be granted such persons only if
                        German nationals in the enemy states are enabled to return to Germany.
                        Kirk.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed> Wilson <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
